# Phaser Audio Management Core

## Context
- When implementing sound effects and music in Phaser games
- When targeting multiple platforms with different audio capabilities
- When setting up the audio architecture for a new Phaser game

## Requirements
- Configure Phaser's sound manager with optimal parameters during game initialization
- Implement a centralized audio manager class to handle all Phaser audio interactions
- Properly preload all audio assets in Phaser's loading scene with multiple formats
- Implement efficient clean-up of audio resources during scene transitions

## Examples

```typescript
// Core audio manager setup for Phaser
export class CoreAudioManager {
  private scene: Phaser.Scene;
  private soundEffects: Map<string, Phaser.Sound.BaseSound> = new Map();
  private music: Map<string, Phaser.Sound.BaseSound> = new Map();
  private sfxVolume: number = 0.7;
  private musicVolume: number = 0.5;
  private muted: boolean = false;
  
  constructor(scene: Phaser.Scene) {
    this.scene = scene;
    
    // Configure optimal audio settings
    this.configureAudio();
    
    // Set up event listeners for game pause/resume
    this.setupEventListeners();
  }
  
  /**
   * Configure Phaser sound manager optimally
   */
  private configureAudio(): void {
    // Access the global sound manager
    const soundManager = this.scene.sound;
    
    // Configure global audio settings
    soundManager.setVolume(1.0);
    soundManager.setMute(false);
    
    // Limit sounds based on platform
    if (this.scene.sys.game.device.os.mobile) {
      soundManager.setMaxListeners(8); // Mobile - fewer sounds
    } else {
      soundManager.setMaxListeners(16); // Desktop - more sounds
    }
  }
  
  /**
   * Set up event listeners for game state
   */
  private setupEventListeners(): void {
    // Handle scene lifecycle events
    this.scene.events.on('pause', this.onPause, this);
    this.scene.events.on('resume', this.onResume, this);
    this.scene.events.once('shutdown', this.shutdown, this);
    
    // Handle global game events
    this.scene.game.events.on('blur', this.onBlur, this);
    this.scene.game.events.on('focus', this.onFocus, this);
  }
  
  /**
   * Preload audio assets with the correct formats
   */
  preloadAudio(): void {
    // Detect browser capabilities for audio format
    const audioTest = document.createElement('audio');
    const formats = {
      ogg: audioTest.canPlayType('audio/ogg; codecs="vorbis"').replace('no', ''),
      mp3: audioTest.canPlayType('audio/mpeg').replace('no', ''),
      m4a: audioTest.canPlayType('audio/mp4; codecs="mp4a.40.5"').replace('no', '')
    };
    
    // Determine preferred formats based on browser support
    const preferredFormats = [];
    if (formats.ogg) preferredFormats.push('ogg');
    if (formats.mp3) preferredFormats.push('mp3');
    if (formats.m4a) preferredFormats.push('m4a');
    
    // Load sound effects with multiple formats
    this.scene.load.audio('jump', preferredFormats.map(format => `assets/audio/jump.${format}`));
    this.scene.load.audio('pickup', preferredFormats.map(format => `assets/audio/pickup.${format}`));
    
    // Load music tracks
    this.scene.load.audio('mainTheme', preferredFormats.map(format => `assets/audio/mainTheme.${format}`));
  }
  
  /**
   * Clean up resources when scene is destroyed
   */
  shutdown(): void {
    // Remove event listeners
    this.scene.events.off('pause', this.onPause, this);
    this.scene.events.off('resume', this.onResume, this);
    this.scene.game.events.off('blur', this.onBlur, this);
    this.scene.game.events.off('focus', this.onFocus, this);
    
    // Stop and destroy all sounds
    this.soundEffects.forEach(sound => {
      sound.stop();
      sound.destroy();
    });
    
    this.music.forEach(sound => {
      sound.stop();
      sound.destroy();
    });
    
    // Clear maps
    this.soundEffects.clear();
    this.music.clear();
  }
  
  // Event handlers
  private onPause(): void {
    this.scene.sound.pauseAll();
  }
  
  private onResume(): void {
    if (!this.muted) {
      this.scene.sound.resumeAll();
    }
  }
  
  private onBlur(): void {
    this.scene.sound.pauseAll();
  }
  
  private onFocus(): void {
    if (!this.muted) {
      this.scene.sound.resumeAll();
    }
  }
}
```

## Initialization Best Practices
- Initialize audio manager in scene create method
- Configure audio manager before loading game assets
- Set up volume controls based on user preferences
- Handle audio suspension on mobile platforms
- Initialize all audio components when transitioning from loading to gameplay

## Platform Considerations
- Detect audio capabilities before loading assets
- Provide fallback formats for cross-browser compatibility
- Reduce simultaneous sounds on mobile devices
- Handle audio interruptions on mobile devices
- Implement audio resumption after interruption

